Title: "Overview"
Id: "7ad33634-c9f0-482e-80da-39d9d7d70c23"

Text: "Type statements use `is`.

```mlg-fragment
X is \\set
f is \\function:on{A}:to{B}
A, B is \\set
```

Predicate-like type checks use `is?` and `is_not?`.

```mlg-fragment
x is? \\set
x is_not? \\empty.set
```

Builtin types start with two backslashes, such as `\\\\type`, `\\\\statement`, `\\\\expression`, `\\\\specification`, and `\\\\opaque`."
Id: "2f73683b-6420-4fe6-8196-3ce83be64464"
